\f1\fs22 Detective Superintendent Hayley Lanning was a good cop in a deformed universe of bad cops. What she knew of Lieutenant Alexander Shakti proved he was a dolt of singular disposition. The rank of lieutenant\'97never before seen in Ulyssian policing, mysteriously floating outside the command chain\'97ought to have raised questions for anyone with the curiosity of bathroom mould (which, in this city, excluded every other detective in the building). But to Hayley\'92s chagrin, Shakti\'92s career had gone largely unexamined.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Well, tax my trust funds, she was examining it now.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Whispers said his assignments came directly from the Commissioner, and Shakti was always dispatched to \'93seal\'94 cases the powers-that-be wanted quietly buried. Hayley was digging in, over a fevered weekend since she\'92d learned Shakti was taking over the Scarlet Shower Surgeon case. Her case. His file history was legendary for its carelessness: incoherent notes from the get-go, copyright-infringing Larson cartoons (mostly cows), finally reduced to dismissive one-liners. The latest, for Travis Teh, didn\'92t even require a scroll:\
