\f2\i \cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Nothing to see here, go back to your homes,
\f1\i0  Hayley thought. And mostly they did, terrified of crossing the son of Eloise Shakti, the rapacious corporate-raiding, arms-dealing poster bitch of Ulyssian values. Shakti was a bubbling centre of collusion and incompetence; Hayley had found a study calling it the \'93Trumpet Effect\'94: people got statistically dumber wherever Shakti appeared.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Public relations celebrity, Lieutenant Alexander Shakti speaking. How may you help me?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Detective Superintendent Hayley Lanning here, Lieutenant.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes?\'94 Shakti replied. Hayley pictured him shrugging with indifference. \'93Which production are you consulting to?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley ground her teeth. He\'92d forgotten her\'97maybe a mercy. She pressed on. \'93I was running the Scarlet Shower Surgeon case,\'94 she said, and hated that her voice made it a question.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Scarlet Shower Surgeon case\'85 You\'92ll have to remind me: what show and episode was that again?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93There\'92s no show,\'94 Hayley said through her teeth. \'93It\'92s real. You framed Anthony Chantara for it.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes. Yes, of course. That case is closed, Detective.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I wondered if you\'92d seen the news this morning\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The news?\'94 Shakti almost spat. \'93No, can\'92t stand the stuff: too low budget, all tell, no show, no MC\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Main Culprit,\'94 Hayley supplied, recalling his last ramble.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Exactly. No story arc, detective. Just random events\'97leaving the audience bewildered and the snacks untouched.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Then you haven\'92t heard?\'94 Hayley interrupted, cursing herself for offering up leverage. Tax! Even I\'92m stupider near him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I always hear, detective.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I meant the new murders.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Ah yes, the murders\'85\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Pathetic.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I\'92ve been busy with the Sarah Jacobson abduction, forgive me for not recalling which show you mean\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It\'92s not a show! It\'92s a real case!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Shakti laughed. \'93Oh, detective.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93There\'92ve been more Scarlet Shower Surgeon since his incarceration. Chantara can\'92t have done them.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Seems you haven\'92t caught the latest news, either. The Elvi broke Chanta out of that PAPER\'94\'97he almost choked on the word\'97\'93facility yesterday.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93He escaped?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You haven\'92t heard?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The Elvi broke him out?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Insurrectionists, every one.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley pressed on. \'93All but one of the murders occurred before yesterday. He couldn\'92t have done those.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I see,\'94 Shakti said, and Hayley cautiously allowed herself to hope logic was breaking through. \'93That\'92s a sticky one,\'94 he mused, as if conceding. Then he brightened: \'93What a plot twist.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley felt her sarcasm furl; this was hopeless. \'93A plot twist?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes, this will make the show much more compelling. I\'92ll have my writers pull all-nighters until they can explain it all. No doubt I\'92ll come out looking brilliant: only Lieutenant Alexander Shakti could have cracked the case and brought Anthony Chantara to justice. Mind you, just between us, I\'92m starting to think the production team isn\'92t up to the job. I might have to fire the whole writing team.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Chantara can\'92t have committed those murders,\'94 Hayley insisted.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93But he must have,\'94 Alexander said as if explaining arithmetic to a pelican with a head injury. \'93Chantara committed all the murders before we apprehended him. And since the subsequent attacks fit the MO, Chantara must have committed those as well.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93That is quite impossible!\'94 Hayley was becoming exasperated.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Please, Detective. The logic is impeccable. You don\'92t expect me to explain logic to a woman, do you?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley fumed. \'93I see. Well, I\'92ve consumed enough of your valuable time.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93A credit to your insight, detective. Don\'92t worry. The professional investigators are already storyboarding these murders for future scripts.\'94
